III. THEORETICAL ANALYSIS AND DESCRIPTION
The AA fusion process is inherently conservative, aiming to retain as much information as possible from all sensors [4], [26]. However, this conservativeness can result in suboptimal information utilization, motivating a deeper analysis from the perspective of IC. This section addresses the conservativeness of the AA fusion process in multisensor systems by focusing on IC changes. It investigates the difference in IC between achieving complete information fusion and the conservative AA fusion approach. This analysis is further extended to sensor fusion scenarios with overlapping FoV.
