IV. DISTRIBUTED JUMP-MARKOV PHD FILTERING
In the process of sensor tracking, new targets continuously enter the FoV. In a single-sensor scenario, the design often involves positing low-probability GCs at potential target locations, such as edges and interiors. In contrast, sensor networks can fully utilize the overlap in sensors’ FoV to rapidly confirm these targets. Consequently, this section leverages the inherent advantages of sensor networks to design the MIC method, aimed at effectively predicting these potential target locations.
