C. Construction of Distributed JMPHD Filtering and Communication Optimization
This section presents the construction of a distributed JMPHD filtering framework and explores strategies for optimizing communication between nodes. The development of a distributed JMPHD filtering scheme that incorporates techniques aimed at minimizing communication overhead [16]. Specifically, the distributed fusion process is divided into the following three stages. The details of fusion algorithm are outlined in Algorithm 2. 1) T-GC Selection: In the process of consensus formation, only the T-GCs participate in the propagation and fusion of information, thereby reducing the communication burden and suppressing false alarms. The selection of T-GC is generally identified by two rules [5].
(1) A rank rule: Specifying the number of T-GCs to be equal to or slightly larger than the initial estimate of targets based on preliminary sensor measurements. This estimate is refined as data updates, with higherweight GCs selected as T-GCs. (2) A threshold rule: Setting a threshold, only those with target existence probability greater than this threshold are identified as T-GCs.
